## To release a new version, edit the version in the two lines below and nothing else.
## Title: |cFF69B4PB’s LuaMemoryMonitor|r 0.4.0
## Author: |cFF69B4PinkBanther|r
## Description: Shows how much memory each add-on uses, ranked in a window on the HUD: what its saved variables and its start-up took, measured while add-ons load, and an estimate of what it holds now. /pbmem shows and hides the window.
## Version: 0.4.0
## APIVersion: 101050 101051
## OptionalDependsOn: LibHarvensAddonSettings>=20106
## SavedVariables: PBsLuaMemoryMonitor_Data

## The settings library is optional: without it the panel is missing and /pbmem still does
## everything. Loading after it costs nothing -- the client runs every add-on's files before the
## first load event, so the events are seen whatever the load order.
## Main.lua comes first so the first reading is taken before the rest of this add-on loads.

Main.lua
lang/strings.lua
lang/$(language).lua
Scan.lua
Window.xml
Window.lua
GC.lua
Settings.lua

